{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 26,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.088,
            0.849,
            0.182
          ],
          "content": "3. Blue and yellow paints are mixed in the ratio of 3 : 5 to produce green paint. To produce 40 mL of green paint, how much of these two colours are needed? To make the paint a lighter shade of green, I added 20 mL of yellow to the mixture. What is the new ratio of blue and yellow in the paint?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.184,
            0.444,
            0.204
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Blue paint used = 15 mL"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.205,
            0.471,
            0.224
          ],
          "content": "Yellow paint used = 25 mL"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.229,
            0.503,
            0.25
          ],
          "content": "Ratio of blue to yellow is 1 : 3."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.259,
            0.848,
            0.317
          ],
          "content": "4. To make soft idlis, you need to mix rice and urad dal in the ratio of 2 : 1. If you need 6 cups of this mixture to make idlis tomorrow morning, how many cups of rice and urad dal will you need?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.322,
            0.412,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Rice needed = 4 cups"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.343,
            0.496,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": "And urad dal needed = 2 cups"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.372,
            0.848,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": "5. I have one bucket of orange paint that I made by mixing red and yellow paints in the ratio of 3 : 5. I added another bucket of yellow paint to this mixture. What is the ratio of red paint to yellow paint in the new mixture?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.453,
            0.592,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Ratio of red paint to yellow paint = 3 : 5"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.481,
            0.569,
            0.517
          ],
          "content": "Part of red paint in the bucket $\\stackrel { \\leftrightarrow } { \\mathrm { i } } \\stackrel { \\mathcal { P } } { \\mathrm { S } } = \\frac { 3 } { 8 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.514,
            0.604,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": "Part of yellow paint in the bucket $\\mathrm{i}s \\equiv \\frac{5}{8}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.551,
            0.624,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": "Since, one bucket of yellow paint is added."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.572,
            0.599,
            0.609
          ],
          "content": "So, quantity of yellow paint $\\frac{5}{8} + 1 = \\frac{13}{8}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.609,
            0.74,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": "Thus ratio of red paint to yellow paint $\\frac{3}{8} : \\frac{13}{8} = 3 : 13.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.66,
            0.288,
            0.68
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 176"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.692,
            0.294,
            0.716
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.725,
            0.847,
            0.782
          ],
          "content": "Anagh mixes 600 mL of orange juice with 900 mL of apple juice to make a fruit drink. Write the ratio of orange juice to apple juice in its simplest form."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.788,
            0.656,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** Ratio of orange juice to apple juice is 600 : 900"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.204,
            0.809,
            0.415,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": "Simplest form is 2 : 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.838,
            0.847,
            0.913
          ],
          "content": "2. Last year, we hired 3 buses for the school trip. We had a total of 162 students and teachers who went on that trip and all the buses were full. This year we have 204 students and teachers. How many buses will we need? Will all the buses be full?"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.867,
            0.928,
            0.886,
            0.949
          ],
          "content": ""
        }
      ]
    }
